Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 856/856] feat(weightless): allow per-model default sampling
 params for steered model

Add WEIGHTLESS_STEER_GENERATION_DEFAULTS (JSON object of sampling
defaults such as temperature/top_p/top_k/min_p) applied only when a
request targets WEIGHTLESS_STEER_MODEL and omits those fields, leaving
the stock served model default sampling parameters untouched.

Wired through BaseServing._default_sampling_params_for across Chat
Completions, Batch Chat Completions, Completions, and Responses
entrypoints so explicit caller fields still take precedence and
SamplingParams validates greedy/top_p combinations normally.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: Allows serving the GLP-steered model at a lower default sampling temperature (e.g. 0.3/0.95) while preserving DeepSeek stock generation defaults (1.0/1.0).
Quality: Zero behavior change on the stock served model or when WEIGHTLESS_STEER_GENERATION_DEFAULTS is unset; explicit request parameters always win.
Tests: pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_glp.py -k steered_generation_defaults (7 passed).
Upstream-status: Local per-model sampling defaults for weightless served model.
